# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values.
# `.env.local` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Both values below are safe to expose in the browser — the anon key is a
# PUBLISHABLE key whose power is bounded entirely by Row Level Security
# policies on your tables. Find them in the Supabase dashboard under
# Project Settings -> API.
#
# NEVER put the `service_role` key in this file or anywhere under src/.
# That key bypasses RLS completely.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://kvnmydvsffjvrsndnawd.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# SERVER-ONLY. Required for full account deletion (/api/account/delete).
# NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ PREFIX — that prefix ships a value to the browser, and this
# key bypasses Row Level Security completely. Anyone holding it can read or
# delete every user's data. Supabase dashboard -> Settings -> API -> service_role.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# SERVER-ONLY. Required for Ask AI (/api/chat).
# NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ PREFIX. An API key shipped to the browser is a public API
# key — anyone can read it out of the JS bundle and spend it. This is exactly
# the bug the original prototype had (a client-side fetch straight to a model
# API) and the reason /api/chat exists as a server route at all.
#
# Currently Gemini 3.7 Flash on the free tier, with a same-provider fallback
# chain to 3.5/3.1 (lib/ai/guard.ts) — a deliberate "no billing yet" choice
# while the app has no users. Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# SERVER-ONLY, OPTIONAL. Powers the resume-text rewrite inside Profile
# Analysis (/api/analysis/resume) — and ONLY that route. Deliberately not
# used for Ask AI or the activities interview: those sit behind the
# crisis/immigration-enforcement guardrails, where a free, unvetted model
# tier is too much risk. Rewriting a student's own activity description
# carries none of that.
#
# Free-tier models only, rotated across several (lib/ai/openrouter.ts) so one
# retired or rate-limited model doesn't take the feature down — same shape as
# GEMINI's fallback chain, but across providers instead of within one. Get a
# key at https://openrouter.ai/keys (no card required for the free tier).
# Leaving this unset is a normal, working state: the route falls back to the
# Gemini chain above with no other change.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Reserved, not read by any route yet. Real-money upgrade path for the
# highest-stakes AI surface once usage justifies billing — deliberately not
# turned on while OpenRouter's free rotation is doing the job. See the
# PROVIDER note at the top of src/app/api/chat/route.ts before wiring it in.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
